<PARA INFOID = "T010257A101" UPDATE = "ORIGINAL" LDUP = "12Dec2003"     INFOTYPE = "PARTS" INDSW = "ON">
<TITLE>Oil Pump</TITLE>
<LIST1 TYPE = "UNORDERED"><ITEM><PTXT>The oil pump is a compact, high-efficiency, multi-tooth cycloid rotor type driven directly by the crankshaft and is located on the timing chain cover. The discharge volume has been optimized, and the drive rotor has a spigotless construction, reducing the rotor diameter and friction loss.</PTXT></ITEM>
<ITEM><PTXT>A relief valve is built in, and a bypass passage is provided so that relieved oil does not return directly to the oil pan, suppressing fluctuations in the oil level in the oil pan and reducing friction.</PTXT></ITEM>
<ITEM><PTXT>FIPG (formed in place gasket) with excellent sealing performance is used on the mounting surfaces with the cylinder block and oil pan to ensure reliability.</PTXT></ITEM></LIST1>
